 "how": "B1955 (main's own recomputation of this note, verification/wa3_on_main.py and class_is_a_choice.py), part E and class_is_a_choice.py: the knot's form V + V^T = [[2, 1], [1, -2]] (determinant -5) gives the discriminant form q = x^2/5, a residue, with bilinear form 2x^2/5; B1951's rho(T) = diag psi(2x^2) is the other class; the unit shears on the labels are implemented by the coefficients 2 and 3, the class of 2x^2/5; the flux-5 modes carry the non-residue class (checks/web_review.py R3); the Weil 3's T-phases are {0, 1/5, 4/5} in one class and {0, 2/5, 3/5} in the other. So the object carries both forms and the class is a choice, as the note's corrected version says and B1955 records (corrected the same day on the seat's referee read)",
